.SH SLURM JSON COLLECTION
Slurm autodetection prefers the legacy slurm backend. Explicit -b slurm_json
selects JSON collection. JSON capability is checked in the first collection;
unsupported clients fall back once with a diagnostic. In watch mode, a
single background collector queries partitions, nodes and jobs every
20 seconds independently of terminal redraws. Failed refreshes retain the
last successful snapshot; scheduler messages show its age and collection span.
Separate Slurm responses are not a globally atomic scheduler snapshot.
The command timeout is configurable with scheduler_command_timeout.

.SH SLURM SUMMARY COLLECTION
.B \-\-slurm-summary
selects the legacy slurm backend and collects only sinfo and squeue on each
normal display cycle. There is no independent 20-second polling interval;
the watch interval and collection/rendering work govern refreshes.
CPU placement may be estimated; per-job GPU indices are unavailable.
Optional allocation-detail traces are ignored during offline replay too.
This option accepts -b slurm or auto, overrides scheduler defaults, respects
\-\-all, and cannot be combined with \-\-slurm-json-squeue.
